# Tropical Kernel Mean Embeddings and Congruence Witnesses

This file develops the theory of maxitive empirical laws over finite sample spaces,
tropicalized kernel mean embeddings via finitely generated feature algebras, and
constructive congruence witness extraction.

## Main Definitions

* `MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw` — a weight function on a finite sample space
* `evalMaxitiveLaw` — evaluation of a law on a feature via supremum aggregation
* `tropicalKME` — the tropical kernel mean embedding
* `AgreesOnGenerators` — predicate for equality of evaluations on a generator set
* `witnessDiscrepancyCount` — number of generators separating two laws
* `congruenceWitnessDist` — distance as discrepancy count
* `findWitness?` — computable witness extraction
* `GeneratedFeatureAlgebra` — closure of generators under pointwise sup

## Main Results

* `witnessDiscrepancyCount_eq_zero_iff` — zero discrepancy iff agreement on all generators
* `exists_generator_witness_of_ne` — constructive witness extraction from disagreement
* `congruenceWitnessDist_eq_zero_iff` — KME equality iff no congruence witness exists
* `findWitness?_spec_some` — soundness of witness search
* `findWitness?_spec_none` — completeness: none iff universal agreement
* `findWitness?_complete` — existential completeness of search
* `evalMaxitiveLaw_sup` — evaluation distributes over pointwise sup
* `agrees_on_generated_algebra_of_agrees_on_generators` — agreement propagates to generated algebra
* `generated_algebra_separation` — separation in generated algebra reduces to generator separation
-/

import Mathlib

noncomputable section

open Finset

/-! ## Core Definitions -/

/-- A maxitive empirical law on a finite sample space `ι` with values in an ordered
    semiring `S` is a weight function `ι → S`. This is the tropical/idempotent analogue
    of an empirical probability distribution. -/
def MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw (ι S : Type*) := ι → S

/-- Evaluate a maxitive empirical law `μ` on a feature `f : ι → S` by taking the
    supremum over the sample space of `μ(i) ⊔ f(i)`. This is the tropical analogue
    of the expectation functional `𝔼_μ[f]` in classical kernel mean embedding theory. -/
def evalMaxitiveLaw
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (μ : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) (f : ι → S) : S :=
  Finset.sup Finset.univ (fun i => μ i ⊔ f i)

/-- Generalized evaluation with a user-supplied binary operation instead of `⊔`. -/
def evalMaxitiveLawWith
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (op : S → S → S) (μ : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) (f : ι → S) : S :=
  Finset.sup Finset.univ (fun i => op (μ i) (f i))

/-- The tropical kernel mean embedding: given a generator set `A`, a law `μ`, and a
    feature `f`, evaluate `μ` on `f`. The generator set `A` restricts the domain of
    interest but does not affect the evaluation itself. -/
def tropicalKME
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (_A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) (f : ι → S) : S :=
  evalMaxitiveLaw μ f

/-- Two maxitive laws agree on a generator set `A` if they evaluate equally on
    every generator. This is the zero-distance predicate for the congruence witness
    framework. -/
def AgreesOnGenerators
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) : Prop :=
  ∀ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f = evalMaxitiveLaw ν f

/-- Count the number of generators in `A` on which laws `μ` and `ν` disagree.
    This is the tropical analogue of the MMD witness count. -/
def witnessDiscrepancyCount
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) : ℕ :=
  (A.filter (fun f => evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f)).card

/-- The congruence witness distance between two laws on generator set `A`,
    defined as the discrepancy count. -/
def congruenceWitnessDist
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) : ℕ :=
  witnessDiscrepancyCount A μ ν

/-- Computable search for a witness feature in `A` that separates `μ` from `ν`.
    Returns `some f` if a separating feature exists, `none` otherwise. -/
def findWitness?
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) : Option (ι → S) :=
  let filtered := A.filter (fun f => evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f)
  if h : filtered.Nonempty then some h.choose else none

/-! ## Generated Feature Algebra -/

/-- The feature algebra generated by a set of generators `A` under pointwise supremum.
    This is the tropical analogue of a finitely generated function algebra. -/
inductive GeneratedFeatureAlgebra {ι S : Type*} [SemilatticeSup S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) : Set (ι → S) where
  | generator (f : ι → S) : f ∈ A → GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A f
  | sup_closure (f g : ι → S) : GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A f →
      GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A g → GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A (fun i => f i ⊔ g i)

/-! ## Key Helper Lemma: Evaluation Distributes Over Pointwise Sup -/

/-
The evaluation functional distributes over pointwise supremum:
    `eval μ (f ⊔ g) = eval μ f ⊔ eval μ g`. This is the algebraic engine
    that drives propagation of agreement from generators to the generated algebra.

    The proof uses the identity `a ⊔ (b ⊔ c) = (a ⊔ b) ⊔ (a ⊔ c)` in any
    semilattice, together with the fact that `Finset.sup` distributes over `⊔`.
-/
theorem evalMaxitiveLaw_sup
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (μ : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) (f g : ι → S) :
    evalMaxitiveLaw μ (fun i => f i ⊔ g i) = evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ⊔ evalMaxitiveLaw μ g := by
  simp [evalMaxitiveLaw];
  rw [ ← Finset.sup_sup ];
  exact Finset.sup_congr rfl fun i _ => by simp +decide [sup_comm, sup_left_comm]

/-! ## Main Theorems -/

/-
**Zero discrepancy characterization.** The witness discrepancy count is zero
    if and only if the two laws agree on every generator in `A`.
-/
theorem witnessDiscrepancyCount_eq_zero_iff
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) :
    witnessDiscrepancyCount A μ ν = 0 ↔
      ∀ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f = evalMaxitiveLaw ν f := by
  simp +decide [ witnessDiscrepancyCount, Finset.ext_iff ]

/-
**Constructive witness extraction.** If two laws do not agree on all generators,
    there exists a specific generator that separates them. This is the finite
    congruence witness principle.
-/
theorem exists_generator_witness_of_ne
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S)
    (hsep : ¬ ∀ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f = evalMaxitiveLaw ν f) :
    ∃ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f := by
  grind +revert

/-
**KME equality characterization.** The congruence witness distance is zero
    if and only if the tropical KME evaluations agree on all generators.
-/
theorem congruenceWitnessDist_eq_zero_iff
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) :
    congruenceWitnessDist A μ ν = 0 ↔
      ∀ f ∈ A, tropicalKME A μ f = tropicalKME A ν f := by
  convert witnessDiscrepancyCount_eq_zero_iff A μ ν using 1

/-
**Witness search soundness.** If `findWitness?` returns `some f`, then
    `f` is a member of `A` and separates `μ` from `ν`.
-/
theorem findWitness?_spec_some
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S)
    (f : ι → S) :
    findWitness? A μ ν = some f →
      f ∈ A ∧ evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f := by
  unfold findWitness?;
  grind

/-
**Witness search completeness (none direction).** `findWitness?` returns `none`
    if and only if the laws agree on every generator.
-/
theorem findWitness?_spec_none
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) :
    findWitness? A μ ν = none ↔
      ∀ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f = evalMaxitiveLaw ν f := by
  unfold findWitness?;
  simp +decide [ Finset.Nonempty ]

/-
**Existential completeness.** If a separating generator exists, then
    `findWitness?` returns some witness.
-/
theorem findWitness?_complete
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) :
    (∃ f ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f) →
    ∃ f, findWitness? A μ ν = some f := by
  unfold findWitness?;
  grind +suggestions

/-! ## Generated Algebra Theorems -/

/-
**Agreement propagation.** If two laws agree on all generators in `A`, then
    they agree on every element of the feature algebra generated by `A` under
    pointwise supremum. This is the tropical congruence propagation theorem.
-/
theorem agrees_on_generated_algebra_of_agrees_on_generators
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S)
    (h : AgreesOnGenerators A μ ν) :
    ∀ f, f ∈ GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A →
      evalMaxitiveLaw μ f = evalMaxitiveLaw ν f := by
  intro f hf; induction hf; aesop;
  rw [ evalMaxitiveLaw_sup, evalMaxitiveLaw_sup, ‹evalMaxitiveLaw μ _ = evalMaxitiveLaw ν _›, ‹evalMaxitiveLaw μ _ = evalMaxitiveLaw ν _› ]

/-
**Generator-level separation.** If any element of the generated feature algebra
    separates two laws, then some generator already separates them. This is the
    contrapositive of `agrees_on_generated_algebra_of_agrees_on_generators`.
-/
theorem generated_algebra_separation
    {ι S : Type*} [Fintype ι] [SemilatticeSup S] [OrderBot S] [DecidableEq S]
    (A : Finset (ι → S)) (μ ν : MaxitiveEmpiricalLaw ι S) :
    (∃ f ∈ GeneratedFeatureAlgebra A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ f ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν f) →
    ∃ g ∈ A, evalMaxitiveLaw μ g ≠ evalMaxitiveLaw ν g := by
  contrapose!
  exact fun h => agrees_on_generated_algebra_of_agrees_on_generators A μ ν h

end